16. Exam Definitions
IS NULL

IS NULL is used to check whether a column contains a NULL value.

IS NOT NULL

IS NOT NULL is used to check whether a column does not contain a NULL value.

IFNULL()

IFNULL() is a MySQL function used to replace a NULL value with a specified value.

COALESCE()

COALESCE() returns the first non-NULL value from a list of expressions.

NULLIF()

NULLIF() returns NULL when two expressions are equal; otherwise, it returns the first expression.

